meta {
  name: Read device server mode
  type: http
  seq: 10
}

get {
  url: {{baseUrl}}/devices/:id/server
  body: none
  auth: none
}

params:path {
  id: {{deviceId}}
}

docs {
  What the boat is actually pointed at, read from its own `GET /server`
  (the portal answers `{mode, host, base}`). The UI uses this to fill the
  PROD/DEV row, so a page reload does not have to guess.

  Proxied over LAN, so it needs a known device ip: 409 when the boat never
  heartbeated on a LAN, 502 when the portal does not answer. From Render it
  cannot work at all (a boat's portal address is private), which is why the
  UI disables the buttons there.
}
